<title>ITALY: DHL Italia sales up, but profits lower in 1996/7.</title>
<headline>DHL Italia sales up, but profits lower in 1996/7.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>DHL International Italia said it increased revenue in 1996/97 by 20 percent to 422 billion lire ($249.8 million) but net profits after tax fell back to 1.45 billion from 2.48 billion in 1995/96.</p>
<p>The higher revenue reflects new services DHL introduced on the Italian market. The fall in net profit came after a change in permitted tax deductions on investments.</p>
<p>Turnover in both DHL Italia's international and domestic services grew at the same rate. The international side accounts for 80 percent of total sales.</p>
<p>DHL started operations in Italy in 1978 and now serves some 200,000 clients. ($ = 1689 Italian Lire) - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
